KG42.register("edges-f9110faa2853b8e706f7a128",{"id":"S-c7f7b3f4e7f58d16","source":"COMP-fe1c33d7a61b4b97","type":"links","target":"COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["13-consensus_product_differentiation"],"assertions":[{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R001::E::v141-c-R001-E001","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","rule_ref":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R001","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"bidding.demand","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C003"],"semantic_review_status":"partial","source":"COMP-fe1c33d7a61b4b97","target":"COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","source_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal","target_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","source_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::coordination.price_signal","target_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::bidding.demand","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Communication of consumer quantity estimates during decentralized RCI negotiation. | Consumer requested-energy quantities in MBED and their iterative RCI updates. | Feasibility of consumer requested quantities in MBED. | Sequence of updates within an RCI iteration, restricted to the requested-energy decision variables of consumers. | Target-setpoint calculation for the consumer branch of decentralized RCI negotiation. | The discussed direct-solution alternative for consumer local MBED subproblems, rather than the implemented RCI gradient update.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"5762c957c1e30bf32a3f88c5300e1c2ea554f976753f29abf67923b5bfc8e4f5","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"M01","source_definition":"The producer's current offered bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a producer's bilateral quantity. The consumer's current requested bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a consumer's bilateral quantity. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the producer's current offered bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a producer and its communication neighbor. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the consumer's current requested bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a consumer and its communication neighbor. Each agent must send its bilateral price estimate to its communication neighbor as part of the prescribed information exchange. Scope: Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration. The participants' separately calculated price estimates for a given bilateral trade must agree, λ_nm = λ_mn. Scope: Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. Condition: After convergence. Reaching optimality through RCI does not require sharing agents' internal production/consumption parameters or product-differentiation criterion parameters. Scope: Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. The iterative process stops when convergence is established; convergence criterion (26) is optional. Scope: Termination of iterative RCI coordination. Condition: When algorithmic convergence is established under the prescribed stopping criteria.","target_definition":"The perceived bilateral price supplies an input to the target requested-power setpoint calculation. Scope: Target-setpoint calculation for the consumer branch of decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: The negotiating agent acts as a consumer. Updating bilateral trading-price estimates precedes updating requested-energy decision variables within each RCI iteration. Scope: Sequence of updates within an RCI iteration, restricted to the requested-energy decision variables of consumers. Different offered prices direct the consumer to try to request as much as possible from the neighbor with the most favorable price and nothing from the others. Scope: The discussed direct-solution alternative for consumer local MBED subproblems, rather than the implemented RCI gradient update. Condition: A consumer directly solves its local subproblem when offered different prices. Requested bilateral quantities are nonpositive under the injection convention. RCI enforces this sign restriction at every iteration using the consumer min projection. Scope: Consumer requested-energy quantities in MBED and their iterative RCI updates. Condition: The agent acts as a consumer. The aggregate requested quantity, represented as the consumer's net power injection, is constrained by the agent's lower and upper power boundaries. Scope: Feasibility of consumer requested quantities in MBED. Condition: The agent acts as a consumer; the restriction concerns feasible power setpoints. The current requested bilateral quantity must be included in the information sent to the neighboring agent. Scope: Communication of consumer quantity estimates during decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each iteration, for a consumer and its neighboring negotiating agent.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The perceived bilateral price supplies an input to the target requested-power setpoint calculation. Scope: Target-setpoint calculation for the consumer branch of decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: The negotiating agent acts as a consumer.","expression":"P_{n(m)}^{k+1} = \\dfrac{\\hat{\\lambda}_{nm} - \\overline{\\mu}_n + \\underline{\\mu}_n - b_n}{a_n}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-X-Pnm"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-T-an","v141-c-R001-T-bn","v141-c-R001-T-lambdahat","v141-c-R001-T-mubar","v141-c-R001-T-mulow"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Different offered prices direct the consumer to try to request as much as possible from the neighbor with the most favorable price and nothing from the others. Scope: The discussed direct-solution alternative for consumer local MBED subproblems, rather than the implemented RCI gradient update. Condition: A consumer directly solves its local subproblem when offered different prices.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e23"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":"995","section":"II-A. Peer-to-Peer Trading","anchor_text":"actual power network (being, e.g., transmission and distribution er grids, or possibly a microgrid),","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To model this trading scheme, the net power injection P_n of each agent n ∈ Ω is split into a sum of bilaterally traded quantities with a set of neighboring agents m ∈ ω_n, i.e., P_n = Σ_{m∈ω_n} P_nm (1). A positive value corresponds to a sale/production and a negative value to a purchase/consumption. The set {P_nm | n ∈ Ω, m ∈ ω_n} is the set of decision variables. To lighten notations P_n is also used for the whole set of transactions of agent n."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":"997","section":"III-A. Structure of the Method","anchor_text":"(10d) he m where λkn = (λknm)m∈ωn is the vector of price estimates of ly agent n at iteration k, p⊤n","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In contrast with to the dual ascent method, the local optimization problem is not solved directly as this may affect the solving of the MBED problem. First of all, solving of the local problem can be computationally costly due to the high number of decision variables per agent. A solution can be to replace that complete solving step with a gradient step and a projection on the feasibility set [5], [19]. Additionally, a direct approach to solve local sub-problems in the MBED will most often results in binary outcomes: when offered different prices, an agent will always try to trade as much as possible from the neighboring agent with the most interesting price and nothing from the others."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e28","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-C. Primal Updates","anchor_text":"problem at iteration k presented in (10) can be expressed as Llocn (pn, λkn, μn, μn) = Cn(pn) + Cn(p","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For any trade between two agents n and m, we define a new price, referred to as the perceived price, through λ̂_nm = λ_nm − c_nm (16) By opposition, the trading reciprocity constraint dual variables (λ_nm) are referred to as trading prices. As an example, in a tax implementation of product differentiation, the perceived price corresponds to the price after tax, while trading prices correspond to the price before tax."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"999","section":"III-C. Primal Updates","anchor_text":"SORIN et al.: CONSENSUS-BASED APPROACH TO PEER-TO-PEER ELECTRICITY MARK The Lagrangian of the relaxe","equation_id":"(18)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The Lagrangian of the relaxed problem has bijective gradient when seen as function of the power setpoints. For each negoti-ated trade (between agent n and m, a target power setpoint can be deﬁne using the inverse gradient, i.e.,\n              ˆλnm −μn + μn −bn\n                                                         (18)\n                   an                       P n(m),k+1 ="},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"999","section":"III-C. Primal Updates","anchor_text":"SORIN et al.: CONSENSUS-BASED APPROACH TO PEER-TO-PEER ELECTRICITY MARK The Lagrangian of the relaxe","equation_id":"(19)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The primal variables are then updated following (19), referred to as P-update (here for a producer),\n  P nmk+1 = max  0, P nmk + fnmk  P n(m),k+1 −P nk       (19)\n... The max operator in (19) is used to enforce the sign constraint of the decision variables and is replaced in the case of a consumer by a min operator."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Communication of consumer quantity estimates during decentralized RCI negotiation. | Consumer requested-energy quantities in MBED and their iterative RCI updates. | Feasibility of consumer requested quantities in MBED. | Sequence of updates within an RCI iteration, restricted to the requested-energy decision variables of consumers. | Target-setpoint calculation for the consumer branch of decentralized RCI negotiation. | The discussed direct-solution alternative for consumer local MBED subproblems, rather than the implemented RCI gradient update.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"bidding.demand","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"]},"paper_scope_note":"The λ update, P update, and required communication of RCI have direct formula basis; only protocol component dependencies are allowed, and the values of k and k+1 or the roles of consumer and producer are not conflated."}}],"assertion_ids":["13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R001::E::v141-c-R001-E001"]});
